dialect protocol
protocol stdio.dxf.diff
version 1
schema stdio.dxf
start record

# P2-FG1: REAL binary diff frame, replacing F6's `print_diff().into_bytes()` text-as-binary
# shortcut (`../🦀️component.rs`'s upgraded `DiffCodec` impl, `#region 🔖️TopLevel`) — per the
# P2-W0 census, 100% of stdio's `DiffCodec` impls were still on that shortcut before this pilot
# ladder; this artifact's own upgrade follows the exact pattern `stdio.json`'s `JsonDiff` set.
#
# `format u8` (`store::pack_rt::OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `flags u8` (a 4-bit presence mask —
# bit0=`header_vars`, bit1=`tables`, bit2=`blocks`, bit3=`entities` — `DxfDiff` has FOUR independently
# optional top-level fields, unlike `JsonDiff`'s single `value`, so a bitmask replaces json's own
# single `has_value` byte) are the two REAL fixed header fields; each PRESENT field's own recursive
# collection-triple/tri-state payload follows as one opaque trailing `bytes` chain — genuinely
# structured, varint/length-prefixed binary at the Rust layer
# (`enc_header_vars_diff_bin`/`enc_tables_diff_bin`/`enc_blocks_diff_bin`/`enc_entities_diff_bin`),
# not re-modeled field-by-field here because `Prim::Ref` unconditionally errors on this kind of
# recursive/nested-collection structure during `walk_protocol` (`protocol-prim-ref-recursion` /
# `protocol-array-of-records`, the recipe's own consolidated gap table — every pilot with a
# collection-triple diff independently hit and worked around the same wall).
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field flags u8
chain payload bytes
